SUMMARY:Ali Wong Live LIVE at Arlene Schnitzer Concert Hall
DTSTAMP:20260803T060032Z
DTSTART:20260807T190000Z
DESCRIPTION:Official TicketsResale Tickets \nAbout the Performer\nAli Wong 
	is an Emmy Award-winning actress\, comedian\, writer\, and producer who ha
	s become one of the most celebrated voices in stand-up comedy. Born and ra
	ised in San Francisco\, Ali broke through with her wildly popular Netflix 
	specials Baby Cobra (2016) and Hard Knock Wife (2018)\, both filmed while 
	she was visibly pregnant — a bold and hilarious choice that became her sig
	nature. \nHer fourth Netflix special\, Ali Wong: Single Lady (2024)\, earn
	ed her a Golden Globe Award and a Critics Choice TV Award nomination. She 
	also starred in and executive produced the acclaimed Netflix/A24 dark come
	dy series Beef (2023)\, for which she won the Emmy\, Golden Globe\, Critic
	s Choice\, and Screen Actors Guild Awards for Best Actress in a Limited Se
	ries. \nAli’s comedy is raw\, confessional\, and unapologetically honest —
	 covering topics from relationships and family life to identity and ambiti
	on with a fearless comedic voice that resonates deeply with audiences worl
	dwide. \nEvent Details\nDate: Friday\, August 7\, 2026 \nTime: 7:00 PM (Do
	ors open 1 hour before showtime) \nVenue: Arlene Schnitzer Concert Hall — 
	1037 SW Broadway Ave\, Portland\, OR 97205 \nTicket Limit: 6 tickets per h
	ousehold \nNote: This is Show 1 of 2 Portland performances. A second show 
	takes place on August 8\, 2026. \nAbout the Venue\nThe Arlene Schnitzer Co
	ncert Hall — lovingly called “The Schnitz” by Portlanders — is one of the 
	Pacific Northwest’s most treasured performance spaces. Situated in the hea
	rt of downtown Portland at 1037 SW Broadway Ave\, this magnificent 2\,776-
	seat venue is part of the Portland’5 Centers for the Arts complex. \nOrigi
	nally constructed in 1928 as the Portland Public Theatre\, the hall was me
	ticulously restored and reopened in 1984. Its stunning Italian Baroque arc
	hitecture\, ornate interior details\, and world-class acoustics create an 
	unforgettable atmosphere for live performances. Every seat in the house of
	fers excellent sightlines to the stage. \nThe venue features orchestra\, m
	ezzanine\, and balcony seating levels\, along with a full bar\, concession
	s\, and accessible seating options. Parking is available in nearby downtow
	n Portland garages\, and the venue is conveniently accessible via TriMet p
	ublic transit. Phone: 503-248-4335. \nWhat to Expect\nAli Wong Live is a f
	ull evening of stand-up comedy featuring Ali’s signature confessional and 
	boundary-pushing humor. Based on recent tour reviews\, the show runs appro
	ximately 60–75 minutes including an opening act. \nExpect Ali at her most 
	personal and hilarious — sharing stories from her life post-divorce\, her 
	experiences as a working mother\, and her unique perspective on modern rel
	ationships and identity. Her comedy is sharp\, relatable\, and delivered w
	ith incredible energy and timing. \nThe Arlene Schnitzer Concert Hall prov
	ides an intimate and elegant setting for this performance. With its except
	ional acoustics and warm atmosphere\, every seat feels close to the action
	. Arrive early to enjoy the beautiful venue and grab a drink before the sh
	ow begins. \nTicket Information\nPrice Range: From $118 (resale prices may
	 vary) \nTickets for Ali Wong’s Portland shows are in high demand — secure
